<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $8.5 bln in May 19 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $8.5 bln in May 19 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $8.5 billion in the May 19 week to $3,901.1 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $6.1 billion to $5,056.1 billion. M-1 was up $1.3 billion to $1,061.9 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,898.7 billion versus $3,902.6 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
